            <ArticleTitle>Bladder Endometriosis: Ultrasound and MRI Findings.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>92-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2484/rcr.v1i3.16</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bladder endometriosis is a rare cause of a localized bladder mass, potentially mimicking a neoplasm at cross-sectional imaging. We present the case of a patient with cyclic pelvic pain and urinary symptoms secondary to bladder endometriosis, with characteristic pelvic ultrasound and magnetic resonance imaging findings. Potential pathological mechanisms are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
